## General 

If you are a new agent read .cursor/project-overview.md to get an understanding of the project, its current state and future direction.

When you make significant changes, take stock of what changes you implemented and see if .cursor/project-overview.md needs to be updated based on the recent changes. 

## Web App

### Rendering
- Prefer server components. Client components should be as small as possible — only for interactivity (forms, dropdowns, auth-gated UI).
- Layouts that gate on async data should be server components when possible to avoid client-side fetch waterfalls.
- Never render a loading spinner for data a parent component already has. Use context or props.

### Data fetching
- If a parent already fetched data and provides it via context, children must consume it — never re-fetch the same data.
- Parallel-fetch independent data (use `Promise.all`), never sequential when requests are independent.
- API routes should not call other internal API routes — call service functions directly.

### Database
- Combine related DB queries into single operations (e.g. one `getProjectRole()` instead of separate membership + admin checks).
- Trace total DB queries per page load before shipping. Flag pages that exceed ~5 queries.
- When adding Firestore queries with compound filters, check if a composite index is needed and document it.

### Auth
- Design auth helpers for the common case. `authenticateRequest()` detects token type (JWT vs hex) to skip unnecessary lookups.
- When adding new authenticated routes, reuse existing auth + membership checks — don't reimplement.
